# ffi/logs/rust/stage3-M2.log
# W3 stage 3: M2 (TaskDetailed in ListTasksDetailedResponse) over P2.1 to P2.5,
# alongside M1. Four arms.
# 2026-09-18
#
# CONFIGURATION (R7)
#   machine        4 vCPU Intel Xeon @ 2.80GHz, 15 GB, Ubuntu 24.04.4, Linux 6.18.44 x86_64,
#                  container, NOT an isolated host. No CPU pinning, no governor control.
#   rust           rustc/cargo 1.94.1, profile release (opt-level 3, lto off, codegen-units 16)
#   MSRV declared  1.88. NOT VERIFIED: no 1.88 toolchain exists in this container.
#   incumbent      prost 0.14.4 (prost-build 0.14.4, protox 0.9.1; no protoc here)
#   binding        the C ABI of design/ABI-v1.md
#   LINKAGE        a cdylib (libak_core.so) resolved by the dynamic linker. Section 4
#                  shows the entry points are undefined imports. A C or C++ host that
#                  STATICALLY links the same core gets a direct call and pays less;
#                  this slice measures the shared-library case, which is what every
#                  managed host does.
#   guard          ON for sections 3 and 5. Section 6 is guard OFF.
#   content set    ascii (design/SHAPES.md). latin1 and wide are NOT measured, so every
#                  string figure here is half a number by that document's own rule.
#   reference      ffi/schema/generated/manifest.json, VALIDATED in stage 1
#
# SHAPE CLASS (design/SHAPES.md), labelled here and not only there, because reports get
# assembled from logs:
#   M1 (P1.x)   REAL     3 scalars, 6 strings, 2 singular nested messages. Leaf element.
#   M2 (P2.x)   REAL     27 fields, 4 repeated string fields, a map<string,string> in a
#                        nested child, depth 3. NON-LEAF element: it fails ABI v1 7.2's
#                        batching predicate, which is the point.
#   P2.4a/b     ADDED ARM, not a payload and not a shape change. 80 elements at 3 and at
#                        150 repeats, whose mean is P2.4 exactly in bytes, elements,
#                        fields and strings. They isolate ABI v1 open decision 5.
#   M6, M7      CONTROL  not built yet. Their rows will be labelled CONTROL when they are.
#
# TWO SHAPE-COVERAGE FINDINGS, reported to the aggregating session, not acted on here:
#   1. design/SHAPES.md line 69 says 'packed repeated enum | M2 | what the real schema
#      actually has'. shapes.json has NO packed enum field anywhere, and M2 has no packed
#      field at all. The only packed fields are on M6, the stated control, and they are
#      int64/double/int32/bool. So the one packed shape the real schema has (3 fields,
#      all enums) is not reachable by this payload set.
#   2. design/SHAPES.md says M2 covers 'nested message, depth up to 6 | the schema's
#      maximum static depth'. The maximum static depth in shapes.json is 3, over every
#      message, not 6: ListTasksDetailedResponse -> tasks:TaskDetailed ->
#      options:TaskOptions -> max_duration:Duration.
#
# WHAT EACH ARM'S BYTE IDENTITY IS CHECKED AGAINST (R2, and the point about independence)
#   prost          prost-build structs, objects from the HAND-WRITTEN builder in
#                  crates/stage1-validate. Independent of everything else here.
#   armonik        facade types, objects from the GENERATED builder, encoded by GENERATED
#                  prost::Message impls. Independent of the prost arm on both.
#   core-native    the same facade values, the generated core traversal, no boundary.
#   core-ffi-rust  the same facade values, THE SAME core traversal, through the C ABI.
#                  NOT independent of core-native: they share the codec, so neither
#                  validates the other. Their agreement proves the BINDING.
#   All four are checked against the manifest, which a third implementation
#   (prost-reflect) validated in stage 1. Section 2 additionally checks that the three
#   facade decoders land on the same VALUE from the same bytes, which byte identity of
#   the encoders does not give.
#
# HAZARDS (R9)
#   - 4 shared vCPUs in a container. Absolutes do not travel; ratios are formed inside
#     one process from rounds interleaved across the arms (R4).
#   - Section 6 (guard off) is a DIFFERENT PROCESS from section 5. prost is carried in
#     both as the in-process control.
#   - The counting build (section 3) is a different build from the timed one.
#   - P2.4 against P2.3 is NOT size-matched, which is why the decision 5 isolation uses
#     the added arms and carries prost through the same arithmetic as a floor.
#   - ASCII only, single-threaded, no allocation or footprint measured.

